# Line endings, declared rather than left to each machine's git configuration.
#
# This exists because of a real corruption. One file's blob had been committed
# with CRLF while `core.autocrlf` was true, so checking it out applied the
# LF-to-CRLF conversion to endings that were already CRLF: every line ending
# became `\r\r\n`, the file doubled in length, and the content still looked
# correct in an editor. It was found only because an edit stopped matching.
#
# `text=auto` puts the decision in the repository instead of in each
# contributor's config: text files are stored LF whatever the working tree
# looks like, so the conversion can never be applied twice.

* text=auto

# Explicitly text, because these are formats where a wrong guess is expensive.
*.py     text
*.ts     text
*.tsx    text
*.md     text
*.yml    text
*.yaml   text
*.json   text
*.toml   text
*.twb    text
*.tmdl   text

# Never touched.
*.png    binary
*.twbx   binary
*.pbix   binary
